 with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Connecticut enters the 2028 presidential race as a Democratic-leaning state with no incumbent on the ballot, since the sitting president is term-limited. No public polls of the state, expert ratings, or prediction-market pricing exist yet, and neither side has reported candidate fundraising, so the picture rests almost entirely on partisanship. Connecticut's eight-point Democratic lean implies a mid-single-digit Democratic margin in a neutral national environment.\n\nThe open seat removes any incumbency advantage for either party, and recent headlines — 2028 primary jockeying, early-state calendar debates, and Democratic concerns about Republican meddling in New England — do not yet point to a specific general-election dynamic. The forecast therefore stays close to the state's underlying lean, with unusually wide uncertainty until polling and named nominees clarify the race.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.8243, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.781, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7754, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7619, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7738, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7843, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7768, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7843, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7811, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.7718, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7751, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7661, "margin": 8.0}]}